{"id":"zip-2004","number":2004,"title":"Remove the dependency of consensus on note encryption","status":"Draft","statusDetail":null,"category":"Consensus","owners":["Daira-Emma Hopwood"],"created":"2024-10-22","license":"MIT","discussionsTo":"https://github.com/zcash/zips/issues/917","pullRequest":"https://github.com/zcash/zips/pull/918","kind":"zip","format":"rst","source":"https://github.com/zcash/zips/blob/main/zips/zip-2004.rst","official":"https://zips.z.cash/zip-2004","updatedAt":"2026-02-10T21:17:45Z","summary":"ZIP 213 6 added the ability for coinbase outputs to be shielded. An unfortunate side effect of this was to make consensus dependent on the details of note encryption. This has unnecessarily complicated the specification and implementation…","words":633,"digest":"77865334dcae7b11a556f8be635bd040cf1326d71a9d8bc63cfef72bf7516e01","headings":[{"id":"terminology","title":"Terminology","level":2},{"id":"abstract","title":"Abstract","level":2},{"id":"motivation","title":"Motivation","level":2},{"id":"requirements","title":"Requirements","level":2},{"id":"specification","title":"Specification","level":2},{"id":"changes-to-the-zcash-protocol-specification","title":"Changes to the Zcash Protocol Specification","level":3},{"id":"deployment","title":"Deployment","level":2},{"id":"reference-implementation","title":"Reference implementation","level":2},{"id":"acknowledgements","title":"Acknowledgements","level":2},{"id":"references","title":"References","level":2}],"body":[{"tag":"h2","children":["Terminology"],"id":"terminology"},{"tag":"p","children":["The key word \"MUST\" in this document is to be interpreted as described in BCP 14 ",{"tag":"sup","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["1"],"href":"#bcp14","id":"footnote-reference-1"}]}," when, and only when, it appears in all capitals."]},{"tag":"p","children":["The term \"network upgrade\" in this document is to be interpreted as described in ZIP 200. ",{"tag":"sup","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["4"],"href":"#zip-0200","id":"footnote-reference-2"}]}]},{"tag":"p","children":["The character § is used when referring to sections of the Zcash Protocol Specification. ",{"tag":"sup","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["2"],"href":"#protocol","id":"footnote-reference-3"}]}]},{"tag":"p","children":["The terms \"Mainnet\" and \"Testnet\" are to be interpreted as described in § 3.12 ‘Mainnet and Testnet’. ",{"tag":"sup","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["3"],"href":"#protocol-networks","id":"footnote-reference-4"}]}]},{"tag":"h2","children":["Abstract"],"id":"abstract"},{"tag":"p","children":["ZIP 213 ",{"tag":"sup","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["6"],"href":"#zip-0213","id":"footnote-reference-5"}]}," added the ability for coinbase outputs to be shielded. An unfortunate side effect of this was to make consensus dependent on the details of note encryption. This has unnecessarily complicated the specification and implementation of consensus rules."]},{"tag":"p","children":["This proposal disentangles note encryption from consensus, by instead requiring coinbase outputs for v6 and later transaction versions to be unencrypted. The disentanglement will be complete once earlier transaction versions are no longer allowed on the network, which is likely to happen in some later upgrade."]},{"tag":"h2","children":["Motivation"],"id":"motivation"},{"tag":"p","children":["In the original design of Zcash, the consensus protocol was carefully isolated from the details of note encryption. This property, which was preserved through the Overwinter, Sapling, and Blossom upgrades, reduces the complexity and attack surface of the consensus protocol. It also potentially allows changes to note encryption to be made outside network upgrades."]},{"tag":"p","children":["A dependency on note encryption crept into the consensus protocol as a result of the changes to support shielded coinbase outputs in ZIP 213 ",{"tag":"sup","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["6"],"href":"#zip-0213","id":"footnote-reference-6"}]},", deployed in the Heartwood network upgrade. These changes added the requirement that it must be possible to decrypt Sapling and Orchard outputs in coinbase transactions using a sequence of 32 zero bytes as the outgoing viewing key."]},{"tag":"p","children":["The complexity impact of this change was overlooked. This became apparent during the design of ZIP 212 ",{"tag":"sup","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["5"],"href":"#zip-0212","id":"footnote-reference-7"}]}," for the Heartwood network upgrade. In fact for a time there were separate and slightly diverging implementations of note decryption for the consensus checks in ",{"tag":"em","children":["zcashd"]},", and in ",{"tag":"em","children":["librustzcash"]},". This could have led to a chain fork between ",{"tag":"em","children":["zcashd"]}," and ",{"tag":"em","children":["zebrad"]}," before the implementations were reconciled."]},{"tag":"p","children":["This ZIP restores the originally intended design property."]},{"tag":"h2","children":["Requirements"],"id":"requirements"},{"tag":"p","children":["The consensus rule change specified in this ZIP must, from transaction version 6 onward, make the implementation and specification of shielded coinbase outputs independent of note encryption."]},{"tag":"h2","children":["Specification"],"id":"specification"},{"tag":"h3","children":["Changes to the Zcash Protocol Specification"],"id":"changes-to-the-zcash-protocol-specification"},{"tag":"p","children":["In § 5.4.3 'Symmetric Encryption', rename ",{"tag":"math","children":[{"tag":"mi","children":["S"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["y"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["m"]}]}," to ",{"tag":"math","children":[{"tag":"mi","children":["N"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["o"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["t"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["e"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["S"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["y"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["m"]}]}," and add the following text:"]},{"tag":"blockquote","children":[{"tag":"p","children":["Let ",{"tag":"math"